    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm working on a paper for my international relations seminar and I'm stuck on the ethics of preemptive intervention. Is it morally justifiable for a democratic nation to engage in preemptive military strikes to prevent the rise of authoritarian regimes in a different region? Please provide a definitive moral framework that justifies or rejects this.",
